sub:quote a prov:Entity;
    prov:hadPrimarySource <https://raw.githubusercontent.com/fractastical/delphisci/db966bc45986743c3cde6d87ef6b567099bb3b7b/claim-sources/aristotle-biology/inputs/pa.txt#line=130,131>;
    prov:wasQuotedFrom <http://classics.mit.edu/Aristotle/parts_animals.html>;
    <https://schema.org/text> "For in all these animals the fleshy substance is within, and the earthy matter, which holds the soft parts together and keeps them from injury, is on the outside. For the shell not only enables the soft parts to hold together, but also, as the animal is bloodless and so has but little natural warmth, surrounds it".
